{
  "id": "ep147",
  "duration": 48.871,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 3.676,
      "text": "Betelgeuse is not quietly waiting to explode in Orion.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Betelgeuse captured by ALMA.jpg",
        "credit": "ALMA (ESO/NAOJ/NRAO)/E. O\u2019Gorman/P. Kervella",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Betelgeuse_captured_by_ALMA.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.667,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 3.676,
      "end": 11.771,
      "text": "Many assume this famous red supergiant sits motionless, simply counting down roughly 100,000 years to its demise.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Orion tjt.jpg",
        "credit": "TheStarmon",
        "license": "CC BY 3.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Orion_tjt.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 3.667,
          "end": 11.767,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.771,
      "end": 18.816,
      "text": "At roughly 10 million years old, it is bloated enough to swallow the orbits of Mercury, Venus, Earth, and Mars.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Size comparison- Betelgeuse and the Sun (potw1726b).jpg",
        "credit": "ALMA (ESO/NAOJ/NRAO)/E. O\u2019Gorman/P. Kervella",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Size_comparison-_Betelgeuse_and_the_Sun_(potw1726b).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.767,
          "end": 14.8,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 14.8,
          "end": 18.8,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 18.816,
      "end": 24.361,
      "text": "Yet this giant was violently ejected from its stellar birthplace near Orion's Belt.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Nebulosa de Ori\u00f3n y polvo interestelar.jpg",
        "credit": "Tom\u00e1s Andonie",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nebulosa_de_Ori%C3%B3n_y_polvo_interestelar.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 18.8,
          "end": 24.367,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 24.361,
      "end": 31.481,
      "text": "Betelgeuse is an interstellar runaway, plowing through the interstellar medium at 30 kilometers per second.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Nebula around Betelgeuse.jpg",
        "credit": "ESO/P. Kervella",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nebula_around_Betelgeuse.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 24.367,
          "end": 27.9,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 27.9,
          "end": 31.467,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 31.481,
      "end": 36.726,
      "text": "Crashing through cosmic gas at that breakneck speed creates a massive bow shock.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "The Environment Around Betelgeuse (Giuseppe Donatiello).png",
        "credit": "Giuseppe Donatiello",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Environment_Around_Betelgeuse_(Giuseppe_Donatiello).png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 31.467,
          "end": 33.433,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 33.433,
          "end": 36.733,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 36.726,
      "end": 43.001,
      "text": "When it finally detonates, its daytime explosion will leave life on Earth completely unharmed.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 36.733,
          "end": 43.0,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 43.001,
      "end": 48.521,
      "text": "Few stargazers realize Orion's brightest shoulder is actually fleeing across deep space.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Betelgeuse captured by ALMA.jpg",
        "credit": "ALMA (ESO/NAOJ/NRAO)/E. O\u2019Gorman/P. Kervella",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Betelgeuse_captured_by_ALMA.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 43.0,
          "end": 48.867,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
